    "standard_name_aliases_reason": "The CNRM ALADIN63 datasets of the clear-sky radiation fluxes (and of reffclwtop) use descriptive names that are not CF standard names; their variables, units and long names are those of the MIP variables with the same name, so they are taken as the CF standard names of the MIP variables (the datasets keep the MIP variables) and reported separately by the check (known_alias). The RegCM4 datasets of the geopotential heights at the pressure levels have the standard name (and long name) of the air temperature, an error in generating the metadata (in RegCM4-3 also the units, see units_errors): taken as the standard name of the geopotential height. The placeholder standard names of the ts of CCAM-1704 (long_name) and of the prc of RegCM4-7 (prc) are those of the MIP variables (see units_errors).",
